  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Let $f$ be the function for which $f(2x+3)=3x+2$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$. Find $f(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{3}{2}x-\\dfrac{5}{2}$.\n\nLet $a=2x+3$ and substitute $x=\\dfrac{a-3}{2}$.",
      "worked": "Let $a=2x+3$, so $x=\\dfrac{a-3}{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(a)&=3\\left(\\frac{a-3}{2}\\right)+2\\\\f(a)&=\\frac{3a-9+4}{2}\\\\f(a)&=\\frac{3a-5}{2}\\\\f(a)&=\\frac{3}{2}a-\\frac{5}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\dfrac{3}{2}x-\\dfrac{5}{2}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
